.TH LOSETUP 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
losetup \- peripheriques boucle / set up and control loop devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B losetup
[-a | -f | -d dev | [-r] [-o offset] dev file]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Attaches a file to /dev/loopN with the LOOP_* ioctls (LOOP_SET_FD, LOOP_SET_STATUS64, LOOP_CLR_FD, LOOP_GET_STATUS64). -a lists, -f prints a free device, -d
detaches, -r read-only, -o byte offset.
.SH SEE ALSO
mount(1)
